    verification markerTextWithoutMarkerHoldsRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "39bfb9be-fa5f-4b42-93ef-807c288d4160"; :>> title = "Sprint 665 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-11"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN: no new Issue this sprint. FINDING 1: the primary stated the history counts (105 marker Decisions, ten prose mentions) in the guard's doc comment and catalogue row BEFORE running the guard; the guard's first run read 104 and 1 - the measurement list had 104 entries and nine of the ten prose hits also carry a marker part, which the guard classifies first. Caught by D0388 applied late: the number a doc states is the number the check printed, never the primary's reading of a script's output. Corrected in the same sprint; no control added because the guard IS the control - the doc numbers are re-read against it here and the self-build test asserts the single history line. FINDING 2: the integration test's first run failed on decision-rationale (a fixture context of one letter), not on the guard under test; the fixture now carries real text and the test asserts the consent-scope row alone, since the other guards' verdicts on a bare scaffold are not this sprint's claim. FINDING 3: the backlog DoD's 'in the record's own acceptance test' was not implemented as written - the header line was chosen because accept_decision owns the {d}Accept Test name - and the deviation is stated in the DoD text above rather than silently absorbed. FINDING 4: the first verifier receipt was RED - clippy 5 errors (doc-comment shape in deck.rs and write.rs) and the lib's own write::atomic_write_tests::no_public_write_reads_outside_the_lock, which read note_marker_hold's read_to_string inside a closure as a public write reading outside the lock; the fix is the module's own idiom (pub fn takes the lock, a private _locked fn reads and writes), which is also what the line-based lint can see. The primary's pre-verifier run had covered neither clippy nor the lib's lint tests - the D0425 split did its job. A sixth lint (too_many_lines on cmd_record, at exactly 100 before the sprint) was masked behind the five and surfaced only once they were fixed; folded with the D0337 marker check into one consent_scope_gate helper, no suppression. FINDING 5: the primary ran cargo fmt on the crate, which this repo does not format with rustfmt (no rustfmt.toml), rewriting 137 files (+28937/-6442); nothing landed - git status showed it before any commit. Recovery: git checkout on the 133 untouched files, then the four sprint files restored from HEAD and the sprint's textpatch scripts replayed, with rustfmt(replayed) == the formatted copy byte-for-byte as the check that every edit was recovered (cmp equal on all five files). Tracked as issue473 with a resolver in the backlog."; }
    part markerTextWithoutMarkerHoldsRetroGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "1107ded6-79ad-4d63-8e95-59ec49e4b67e"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "0986b7a"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-10"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
